%% @fig 02
%% @kicker The cross-encoder
%% @alt The query and one candidate document go into the cross-encoder as a single combined input, so every query token can attend to every document token. The model reads the pair side by side and outputs one relevance score.
%% @caption One model reads the query and the document together, which is why its score is accurate and why it's too slow for the whole corpus.
